<title>USA: VEBA AG unit to buy Wyle for $810 million.</title>
<headline>VEBA AG unit to buy Wyle for $810 million.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Electronics distributor Wyle Electronics has agreed to be acquired by a subsidiary of the German utilities giant VEBA AG in a deal worth $810 million, the companies said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Under the agreement, approved by the boards of both companies, VEBA's Raab Karcher AG unit will pay $50 cash for each Wyle share.</p>
